96 0 obj
  << /ActualText (This artwork means a lot to me\056 It was the breaking point of my own personal art Journey\056 \nDuring my teenage years\054 studying art in school\054 I had become ridgid\056 I lost the freedom of exploration I had as a child\054 the thing that always brought me the most joy when creating\056 For some years I barely even created anything\056\nThis particular piece came from a moment of a lot of strong emotions about self identity\054 that needed to be let out in some way\056 \nI just sat down\054 forgot all my usual worries of \042will it look good to other people\042 or \042is this the right way to do it\042 and just drew\056 \nThe lines are messy\054 I used as many materials as I felt like to make it look right\054 not to someone else\054 but just to me\056 \nI just felt\054 and did\056 No thinking\056 \nThe artsyle I used for these self portraits was so different from my usual attempts of portraits\054 that I was never quite happy with\056 \nAt the same time i realised that it\047s okay to change my mind\056 The paper on the right side originally had text written under it\054 that I didn\047t lik)
     /K [ 0 ]
     /P 95 0 R
     /Pg 92 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
